 - The unit of adoption is a tab, inside an adopted workspace. `teamspace adopt` binds a workspace and adopts no tabs; `seat adopt` binds one tab and one clone per agent pane. Unmanaged tabs in an adopted workspace are never closed, renamed or reused.
 - Live facts (workspace, tab, pane ids, observed harness, model and args, the pane's threads seat) are gathered at admission and carried in the plan args. The mutation rechecks at apply that the pane still has the same owner, and refuses a seat already held by another clone.
 - Adopted clones are keyless: no `threads.reserve_key` want, no key link and no key in the launch environment. The start and restore gates in the planner and the threads effects treat `keyless` as launchable without a reservation; the seat comes from what threads hands the pane.
+- After a Herdr restart the planner wants `threads.rebind_held_seat` (`ResurrectSeat` with no `replace` on the seat's own pane, op key `rebind:<clone>:<incarnation changed_at>`) on every pass while a seated clone's fact, read in the current incarnation, is `Unresolved` and its bound pane exists, including after the grace; the first such read records `seat_unresolved:<clone>`, and a definitive refusal is recorded once as `rebind_refused:<clone>` and not retried in that incarnation. A fresh start of a seated keyless clone waits until the seat is placed in this incarnation or the 90 s grace since `incarnation:changed_at` ends, whatever the rebind did; a fresh keyed start never waits. A `RelaunchOccupant` (the resume driver's relaunch), keyed or keyless, waits out the full grace; placement does not release it. `restart_covered` counts a `launched:` meta as having had an agent. A seat still `Unresolved` when the grace ends is listed under `clones.restart_held` (doctor `restart held`) with the reason and the operator remedy `herdr-threads human seat rebind SEAT --pane PANE --operator`; the row clears when the seat resolves.
 - A mixed tab is allowed: a pane with no agent stays unmanaged inside the seat's tab, and the plan warns that closing the tab closes it. Agent panes of different harnesses, or a `--harness` that contradicts the agents, are refused.
 - Release is a retirement with mechanism `released` and has no Herdr effect. The reconciler skips a released teamspace's workspace and ignores a released object's token, and the threads wants of a released clone are empty: its Required invitations are released and nothing else in threads is touched.
 - Only adopted objects can be released (checked against the live `adopt` action). Undo of an adoption is a release.
 - The node manager can be released (or its adoption undone) only while it is the graph's only live seat; the release clears `node_manager_seat` to unassigned as a listed `graph.node_manager_seat` effect, so the next adopted or created seat becomes node manager. With another live seat the release is refused and the message says to move the role first (`node-manager set`); `teamspace release` follows the same rule over the seats it releases. A release supersedes the live adopt actions of what it releases (the op goes into `undone_by`), so they leave the `undo` list.
